{
  "body": {
    "content": [
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Chả cá Lã Vọng is one of Hanoi's most celebrated dishes. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Firm white fish is marinated in turmeric and galangal, then sizzled in a pan with masses of dill and spring onion. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "This recipe serves 4.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Traditionally this dish is cooked at the table in a small pan over a burner. You can replicate it at home by cooking in a very hot pan and serving immediately.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What you need",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "chicken-breast",
              "amount": 600,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "use firm white fish such as cod or haddock, cut into 4 cm pieces",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "fish"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "turmeric-ground",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "ginger-fresh",
              "amount": 30,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "finely grated",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "fish-sauce",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "shallots",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "finely sliced",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "marinade"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vegetable-oil",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "dill-fresh",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "large bunches",
              "prepNote": "roughly chopped",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "herbs"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "spring-onion",
              "amount": 6,
              "unit": "whole",
              "prepNote": "cut into 5 cm lengths",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "herbs"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "noodles-rice",
              "amount": 300,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "cooked",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "to serve"
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "peanuts",
              "amount": 60,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "roasted",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": "to serve"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Method",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Mix the turmeric, ginger, fish sauce, and sliced shallots in a bowl. Add the fish pieces and toss gently to coat. Cover and refrigerate for at least 2 hours.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Cook the rice noodles according to the packet. Drain and keep warm.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Heat the oil in a large frying pan over high heat until very hot. Remove the fish from the marinade and shake off any excess.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Add the fish in a single layer. Fry for 3 to 4 minutes without moving until golden and crusted. Turn carefully and cook for another 2 to 3 minutes.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Push the fish to one side. Add the spring onion and dill to the pan and toss in the hot oil for about 1 minute until wilted.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Serve the fish and herbs immediately over the warm noodles. Scatter the roasted peanuts on top.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Mix a little ",
                    "type": "text"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "mắm tôm ",
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                        "attrs": {
                          "termSlug": "mam-tom-term"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "with lime juice and sugar as a dipping sauce if you can find it, or serve with fish sauce and chilli on the side.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
              }
            ],
            "type": "listItem"
          }
        ],
        "type": "orderedList"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Do not touch the fish for at least 3 minutes. It will release from the pan naturally once a golden crust forms.",
              "cause": "The fish was moved too soon before a crust formed.",
              "symptom": "The fish breaks apart when turning."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "This is normal. Use a pan you do not mind staining and open a window. The strong smell means the spice is blooming correctly.",
              "cause": "Turmeric is very pigmented and aromatic when heated in oil.",
              "symptom": "The turmeric stains the pan and makes the kitchen smell strong."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "fix": "Add the herbs at the very end. Toss for 30 to 60 seconds only. Serve immediately before the herbs overcook.",
              "cause": "The pan was too hot for too long after the herbs were added.",
              "symptom": "The dill wilts too fast and turns limp."
            }
          }
        ],
        "type": "troubleshooter"
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Where this dish lives",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Chả cá Lã Vọng is named after a street in Hanoi's Old Quarter that is dedicated to this single dish. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Several generations of one family ran the original restaurant before the name spread. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "Hanoi locals eat this dish with mắm tôm, which gives it a very pungent and distinctive flavour. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "The combination of turmeric and large amounts of fresh dill is unusual in Vietnamese cooking. ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "It is considered one of the greatest dishes in Vietnamese cuisine.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      }
    ],
    "type": "doc"
  },
  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "definition": "A pungent Vietnamese fermented shrimp paste. It is diluted with lime juice and sugar to make a dipping sauce served with chả cá.",
      "term": "Mắm tôm",
      "slug": "mam-tom-term"
    }
  ],
